<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Navarro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1460–<a href="/years/1528">1528</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Navarro was a Navarrese soldier and military engineer famous for his use of mines in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-warfare">siege warfare</a>. In Spanish service he commanded the troops that took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a> in 1509, and in 1510 he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a> and Tripoli on the North African coast. Later captured by the French, he served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and died a prisoner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-navarro.jpg" alt="Pedro Navarro" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Pietro_Navarro._Wellcome_M0006758.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
